threadpool: destroy pool before jg2 vhost at PROTOCOL_DESTROY, fixes F-001

From: Andy Green <andy@warmcat.com>

Workers still inside jg2_ctx_fill() walk ctx->vhost, and the done-queue
reap at threadpool destroy runs each task cleanup, which destroys its
jg2_ctx and locks vhost->lock.  Freeing the vhost (incl.
git_libgit2_shutdown) before those joins and cleanups was a shutdown-
window UAF for any in-flight job, e.g. an unauthenticated long blame
held open across a daemon restart.  Join and reap first, then tear the
vhost down.
---
 src/protocol_gitohashi.c |   10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/protocol_gitohashi.c b/src/protocol_gitohashi.c
index dc9e24a..a200401 100644
--- a/src/protocol_gitohashi.c
+++ b/src/protocol_gitohashi.c
@@ -455,9 +455,17 @@ callback_gitohashi(struct lws *wsi, enum lws_callback_reasons reason,
 			lwsl_err("%s: NULL vhd\n", __func__);
 			break;;
 		}
-		jg2_vhost_destroy(vhd->jg2_vhost);
+		/*
+		 * A worker still inside jg2_ctx_fill() is walking
+		 * ctx->vhost, and the threadpool done-queue reap destroys
+		 * each task's jg2_ctx, which locks vhost->lock.  The
+		 * threadpool destroy joins the workers and runs those
+		 * cleanups, so it has to complete while the vhost is still
+		 * alive -- only then can the vhost itself go away.
+		 */
 		lws_threadpool_finish(vhd->tp);
 		lws_threadpool_destroy(vhd->tp);
+		jg2_vhost_destroy(vhd->jg2_vhost);
 		vhd->jg2_vhost = NULL;
 		break;
 
